  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Jagat Singh vs State Of U.P. on 10 July, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 82 Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 15308 of 2020 Applicant :- Jagat Singh Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Pankaj Kumar Gupta Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J. Order on the Exemption Application Application is allowed.",
    "facts": "Offence under section 60 of Excise Act is bailable and triable by Magistrate.",
    "arguments": "learned A.G.A. Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, I.P.C. is unjustified. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 25.4.2020, who is not a previous convict. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the bail prayer of the applicant. Keeping in view the nature of the offence, argument advanced on behalf of the parties, spreading of novel corona virus in jails, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate Jagat Singh vs State Of U.P. on 10 July, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/166316638/ 1 of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22",
    "petitioner_arguments": "learned A.G.A. Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272, I.P.C. is unjustified.",
    "respondent_arguments": "False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 25.4.2020, who is not a previous convict. Learned A.G.A. has opposed the bail prayer of the applicant. Keeping in view the nature of the offence, argument advanced on behalf of the parties, spreading of novel corona virus in jails, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate Jagat Singh vs State Of U.P. on 10 July, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/166316638/ 1 of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22",
